1. Only share what’s required
   - Most forms only need the last 4 digits. If the requester asks for full SSN, ask why and whether a partial (last 4) is acceptable.

2. Prefer secure channels
   - Use the organization’s secure upload portal, encrypted web form, or an encrypted email/file-transfer service. Don’t send full SSNs over plain email or unprotected attachments.

3. If you must redact on a scan, do it properly
   - Don’t just draw a black box over the text in a PDF or image and save — underlying text or OCR can still expose it.
   - Use a true “redaction” feature (e.g., Adobe Acrobat Pro’s Redact tool) which removes the content permanently before saving.
   - If you only have images: open the image in an editor, paint over the SSN, then export/save as a new flattened image (and recreate the PDF from that image). Verify you cannot select or copy the redacted numbers.
