- For PDFs with selectable text: use a proper PDF redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro's Redact tool). Mark the text to redact, Apply Redactions, then use "Remove Hidden Information" and Save As a new file. This permanently removes the hidden text.
- If you only have basic tools: open the PDF as an image (print to PDF or export as image), redact the image, then save — but verify the original text is gone.

3) Verify redaction
- Try to select/copy the redacted area. If you can copy the full number, the redaction is not secure.
- Open the file in a text editor or run a text search (for PDFs) to ensure the digits do not exist in the file.
- Check/remove metadata/EXIF from images and PDFs (some tools strip metadata on export; Acrobat has "Remove Hidden Information").

4) Safer ways to send a full SSN if necessary
- Use the organization’s secure portal or encrypted upload.
- If emailing, send a password-protected PDF (use a strong password) and transmit the password in a separate channel (text/call).
- Use end-to-end encrypted email (PGP/SMIME) if both parties support it.
- Consider sending by certified mail or delivering in person if possible.

5) Minimize risk
- Only share SSN with trusted, verified recipients for necessary purposes.
- After sending, monitor accounts and credit for unusual activity. Consider a credit freeze or fraud alert if you think the SSN may be exposed.

