Short answer: only share what the form actually requires, and if you must send the full SSN, use a secure channel. If the form only asks for the last four digits, redact the first five digits before you scan/send.

Practical guidance and a short checklist

1) What to show
- If the form explicitly asks only for the last 4 digits: redact the first five (display as XXX-XX-6789).
- If the form requires the full SSN: provide it, but only via a secure method (see below). Don’t send the full SSN over unencrypted email or publicly accessible links.

2) How to redact (physical documents)
- Use a permanent black marker to fully cover the first five digits.
- Then make a photocopy or rescan the redacted page and confirm the covered numbers cannot be read or seen through the paper.
- Keep the original secure (shredded when no longer needed).

3) How to redact (digital files)
- Use a proper redaction tool (e.g., Adobe Acrobat Pro “Redact” feature) that permanently removes the underlying text — not just a black box overlay.
- If you edit an image, crop or permanently paint over the pixels and save/flatten the file (export as a flattened PDF or PNG/JPEG).
- Remove document metadata/OCR layer that might contain the SSN.
- Do NOT just place a black shape over text in a PDF without flattening — that can sometimes be reversed or revealed.

4) Secure transmission
- Use the organization’s secure upload portal whenever possible.
- If you must email, send a password-protected PDF (AES-256) and send the password by a separate channel (text or phone).
- Alternatively use an encrypted file-transfer service or secure message feature (SFTP, secure client portal).
- Confirm recipient identity before sending.

5) Minimize exposure and keep records
- Only send the minimal required pages (avoid sending extra documents that include SSN).
- Ask the recipient how they will store/secure the document and how long they’ll keep it.
- Keep a copy of what you sent and when; delete drafts with sensitive info.

6) If you’re unsure
- Contact the organization and ask whether an upload portal exists or whether providing only the last four digits is acceptable. Ask for confirmation of secure handling.

