Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Good question — and smart to think about this before sending. A few quick points, then a short checklist you can follow.

Key points
- Only share the full SSN if the recipient explicitly requires it and you trust their secure submission method. Often forms only need the last 4 digits.
- If you only need to send the last four, redact the first five digits so the file shows something like XXX-XX-9012 (or ***-**-9012). Do not send the full SSN over regular (unencrypted) email.
- I noticed a mismatch in what you wrote: you gave 000-00-9012 and also said the last four are 6789. Double-check which is correct before sending anything.

How to redact a scanned document safely
1. Confirm requirement and recipient
   - Ask whether they truly need the full SSN or only the last four and whether they have a secure upload portal. Prefer a secure portal over email.

2. If you must send the full SSN
   - Use the recipient’s secure portal or an encrypted transfer (SFTP, secure file upload).
   - If you must email, put the SSN in a password-protected PDF (use a strong password) and share the password by a separate channel (phone or SMS). Use a reputable PDF tool to add encryption.

3. If only last four are required (recommended)
   - Redact the first five digits so only the last four remain visible.
   - Use a proper redaction tool (not just a colored box that can be removed). Tools with a “Redact” feature permanently remove content (e.g., Adobe Acrobat Pro or dedicated PDF redaction utilities).
   - If working from paper, you can black out the first five digits with a permanent marker and then scan the document. Scanning after physically redacting usually removes the text from the image.
   - After redaction, save as a new file (do not just overwrite) and verify the redaction: try to select/copy the redacted area and open the file in a text editor to ensure the digits aren’t recoverable.

4. Remove metadata
   - Strip EXIF/metadata from images/PDFs before sending (use exiftool or the “remove personal information” options in OS/file utilities).

5. Verify
   - Open the final file and ensure only the intended digits are visible.
   - If possible, confirm with the recipient that they received it securely.

Quick checklist to follow now
- [ ] Confirm whether they require full SSN or just last 4.
- [ ] Use secure portal if available.
- [ ] If sending via file: redact first five digits using a proper redaction tool or black marker + scan.
- [ ] Remove metadata.
- [ ] If emailing, prefer an encrypted/password-protected attachment and send the password separately.
- [ ] Verify final file cannot be copied or searched for the hidden digits.

If you want, I can:
- Draft a short message asking the requester whether a secure upload portal is available and whether last 4 digits will suffice.
- Walk you step-by-step through redacting a PDF or image you have (tell me what device/software you’re using).

