Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Short answer: Yes—unless the recipient explicitly requires the full SSN and provides a secure upload method, you should redact the SSN so only the last four digits are visible (for example: XXX‑XX‑6789). Never send the full number over an insecure channel like regular email.

Practical guidance and checklist

1) Decide whether the recipient truly needs the full SSN
- Ask the recipient (HR, bank, agency) whether they will accept only the last four digits on a scanned copy or whether they require the full number on the form.
- If they require the full SSN, ask for a secure upload portal or encrypted transfer instructions.

2) Best redaction practice (digital)
- Use a proper PDF redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro, Foxit, PDF-XChange, or built-in redaction in enterprise document systems).
- Steps in Adobe Acrobat Pro: Tools → Redact → Mark for Redaction (select the digits) → Apply Redactions → Sanitize Document / Remove Hidden Information. This permanently removes the underlying text and metadata.
- After redaction, try copying text from the PDF or searching for the SSN digits to confirm they’re gone.

3) If you’re using Mac Preview or similar
- Annotations (a black rectangle) often only cover visually and do not remove the underlying text layer. After placing the rectangle, “Print” → “Save as PDF” or “Export as PDF” to flatten layers, then verify the digits cannot be copied or searched. When in doubt, use a dedicated redaction tool.

4) If working from a paper copy
- Best: Make a photocopy and redact the copy (black marker) then scan the redacted copy.
- Avoid writing on or permanently altering an original if you may need it.

5) Secure transmission
- Use the recipient’s secure portal whenever possible.
- If you must email, password-protect the PDF (strong password) and send the password via a separate channel (phone call, SMS, or different email). Note password-protection is not as strong as a secure portal but is better than plain email.
- Alternatively use encrypted email or a secure file transfer service.

6) Remove metadata and hidden text
- Run “Remove Hidden Information” / “Sanitize” in Acrobat or equivalent so no copies of the original SSN remain in metadata or OCR text layers.

7) Verification and cleanup
- After sending, confirm the recipient received the redacted file and that it’s acceptable.
- Delete any unredacted copies from your computer, cloud storage, and trash/recycle bin. If you made a physical copy with the full SSN, store or shred it securely.

8) What to show on the scanned copy
- If allowed: show only the last four digits in place (XXX‑XX‑6789) or black out all but the last four digits.
- Don’t show the full SSN unless explicitly required and transmitted via a secure channel.

If you want, I can:
- Draft a short message you can send to the recipient asking whether a redacted copy (last four only) is acceptable and requesting a secure upload link.
- Walk you step-by-step through redacting a PDF using a specific tool (tell me which tool or OS you’re using).

