Two quick notes before advice: I noticed the numbers you pasted conflict (000-00-9012 vs “last four: 6789”). Please don’t paste your full SSN into chat. I won’t store it, but it’s safer not to share it here. Below are safe, practical steps for redacting SSNs before sending a scanned document.

1) Confirm what’s actually required
- Ask the requester if they truly need the full SSN or only the last four digits. Many forms only require the last 4.
- If the full SSN is required, ask whether there’s a secure upload portal or encrypted email method you should use.

2) If you only need to send the last 4 digits
- Provide only the last 4 digits (e.g., “****-**-6789”) and remove or redact the rest.

3) Redaction methods (physical documents)
- Use an opaque permanent black marker to cover the SSN, then photocopy or scan the redacted copy. Do NOT just use whiteout tape/label that can be removed.
- After scanning, verify the covered area is not readable or visible in the scan.

4) Redaction methods (digital documents / PDFs / images)
- Use a proper redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro’s Redact tool, or other PDF redaction features). Apply redaction and save/export — this removes underlying text, not just hides it.
- If you don’t have a redaction tool: open the PDF/image, paint a solid black box over the SSN, then “flatten” the file (print-to-PDF or export a new PDF) so the original text layer is gone.
- For images, edit in an image editor, draw a black box, save a new file, and avoid keeping the original unredacted file.

5) Check for hidden data
- After redaction, search the saved file for the SSN to make sure it’s not still present in metadata or hidden text.
- Remove metadata (Document Properties) or use a “sanitize” feature if available.

6) File names and thumbnails
- Don’t include the SSN in the file name. Also check thumbnail previews (some mail clients show an image preview) to ensure the SSN isn’t visible there.

7) Secure transmission
- Prefer the requester’s secure upload portal. If you must email, use encrypted email (S/MIME/PGP) or password-protect the PDF and share the password by a different channel (phone or text).
- Turn off auto-save to cloud services that may keep unredacted copies.

8) Keep a careful record
- Retain a copy of what you actually sent (redacted version) and securely delete any unredacted files you no longer need. Empty your recycle/trash and any cloud trash.

9) Other tips
- If mailing a physical copy, you can cut out the SSN section and mail the rest if that’s acceptable for the form.
- If unsure about legal requirements, ask the requester’s HR/records team or check their privacy policy.

Quick checklist to follow now
- Confirm whether full SSN is required.
- Redact with a permanent black marker (physical) or proper PDF redaction tool (digital).
- Flatten/export to remove layers; strip metadata.
- Rename file without SSN and avoid exposing it in previews.
- Send via secure portal or encrypted email / password-protected file.
- Delete any unredacted copies.

If you’d like, I can:
- Draft a short message to the requester asking whether a secure upload or only the last 4 digits are acceptable.
- Give step‑by‑step redaction instructions for Acrobat, Preview (macOS), or a common free tool—tell me which you use.

