I won’t repeat the full SSN you wrote here, but I can tell you what to do.

Key principles
- Never send a full SSN over unencrypted email or untrusted channels unless the recipient explicitly requires it and provides a secure upload method.  
- If the form only needs the last four digits, send only the last four and redact the rest. The last four are commonly acceptable for verification; confirm with the recipient first.  
- Redaction must be permanent — don’t rely on simply covering numbers with a black box annotation or a sticky note in a scanned copy (these can be removed or the underlying text may remain). Use proper redaction or destructive editing.

How to redact safely (quick options)
1. Physical redaction before scanning (simple and reliable)
   - Make a photocopy of the document.
   - Permanently black out the unwanted digits on the paper copy with an opaque permanent marker (cover completely).
   - Scan the marked copy (scan the redacted copy, not the original).  
   - Verify the scan does not show the covered digits under different viewing/contrast settings.

