Short answer: Yes — redact any part of your SSN that the recipient does not explicitly need. If the form only asks for the last four digits, redact the first five digits before scanning or sending. If the recipient requires the full SSN, use secure transfer methods and confirm they need the whole number.

Practical steps and best practices
- Determine necessity: Ask the recipient whether they truly need the full SSN or whether the last four digits will suffice. Only provide the minimum required.
- Redaction method (digital):
  - Use a proper redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro: Tools → Redact → Mark for Redaction → Apply) so the removed text is permanently removed from the file and not just hidden.
  - After redaction, save a new file and verify there’s no selectable/hidden text under the redaction (zoom in, try selecting or running OCR).
- Redaction method (paper):
  - Black out the unwanted digits with a solid permanent marker, then scan the document.
  - Better: make a photocopy, redact the copy, then scan the redacted copy. Shred the original or securely store it.
- If you must send the full SSN:
  - Use a secure upload portal, encrypted email, or secure file-transfer (SFTP, secure client portal). Don’t send full SSNs in plain email attachments if you can avoid it.
  - If you must email a sensitive attachment, password-protect the PDF and send the password through a different channel (text/call).
- Strip metadata: remove file metadata/hidden data (Document Inspector in Office, remove EXIF from images) before sending.
- Verify the recipient and retention policy: confirm who will store the document, how long they’ll keep it, and how it will be protected.
- Disposal: securely delete temporary files and shred any physical copies you no longer need.

Quick checklist before sending
- Does the recipient actually need the full SSN? If not → redact first five digits.
- Redaction performed with a tool that permanently removes underlying text.
- File is saved as a new, checked file (no hidden text or metadata).
- Send via secure channel or encrypt/password-protect and share password separately.
- Confirm recipient’s handling and retention policies.

If you want, I can:
- Walk you through redacting a specific PDF (tell me whether you have Acrobat, Preview on Mac, or need free tool suggestions).
- Draft a message to ask the recipient whether the full SSN is required and what secure method they prefer.

