Short answer: yes — generally you should avoid sending your full SSN in a normal (unsecured) email or scan unless the recipient explicitly requires the full number and provides a secure upload method. In most cases showing only the last four digits is sufficient.

Details and practical steps

1. Confirm what the recipient actually needs
- Ask whether they need the full SSN or only the last four digits. Many forms only require the last 4.
- Ask for a secure upload method (secure portal, encrypted email, or an instructions page) if they say they need the full SSN.

2. If you can provide only the last four digits
- Redact (hide) the rest of the SSN so the attachment shows only the last four digits (e.g., ***-**-9012 or “XXX-XX-9012”).
- That is the safest default if the form or recipient accepts it.

3. If you must send the full SSN
- Use a secure channel: the organization’s secure portal is best. If you must send electronically, use end-to-end encrypted email or a password-protected PDF and share the password by a different channel (phone or text).
- Ask the recipient how they will store/secure the document and how long they’ll keep it.

4. How to redact properly (important)
- Do NOT just add a black box overlay in Word, an image viewer, or a cloud preview — overlays can sometimes be removed and the underlying text recovered.
- Proper redaction methods:
  - Use a PDF redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro “Redact” tool or similar). Apply redactions and save a new file; then “sanitize” or remove hidden metadata.
  - If working with images, permanently erase pixels (edit and save to a new image file). Opening and re-saving as a flattened image (PNG/JPEG) after erasing is fine.
  - If you redact on paper, use an opaque black marker, then scan the marked page. Make sure the original unmarked digital file is deleted.
- After redaction, verify the redacted values cannot be selected/copied and check document metadata for residual copies of text.

5. Additional precautions
- Limit other identifying info in the attachment (avoid sending full name + SSN + DOB all together unless required).
- Keep a record of what you sent and who you sent it to.
- If you suspect a mistake or exposure, contact the recipient immediately and consider a credit freeze or identity monitoring.

6. I noticed a mismatch in what you wrote
- You mentioned “000-00-9012” and also “last four: 6789” — those don’t match. Double-check which last four you mean before sending.

