Short answer: yes — unless the recipient explicitly requires the full SSN, you should redact all but the last four digits before sending a scan. If the full SSN is required, don’t send it over unsecured channels — use a secure portal or encrypt the file.

Details and practical steps

1) Decide whether the recipient really needs the full SSN
- If the form or organization only asks for “last 4,” supply just the last four digits.
- If they explicitly require the full SSN (e.g., some tax, payroll, or background-check forms), follow the secure-transmission guidance below.

2) How to redact correctly (don’t just cover it visually in a PDF)
- Use a true redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro’s Redact tool, PDF editors with redaction features). Redaction permanently removes underlying text and metadata.
- If you only have an image (JPG/PNG), open it in an image editor, draw a solid black box over the digits, then export/“flatten” to a new file (so the hidden data is gone). After that, save to PDF or image.
- Never rely on a simple black rectangle placed on top of selectable text in a PDF without using a redaction/flatten step — the underlying text may still be recoverable.
- After redacting, check by selecting text (if selectable) or running OCR to confirm the SSN cannot be recovered.
- Remove any SSN from the filename and from the email subject/body.

3) If you must send the full SSN, use a secure method
- Preferred: upload through the organization’s secure portal (many employers, banks, government sites offer this).
- If sending a file: password-protect the PDF with strong password (or use an encrypted archive like 7-Zip AES-256) and send the password by a different channel (e.g., call or separate text).
- Alternatively use secure file transfer (end-to-end encrypted service) or encrypted email (S/MIME/PGP).
- Confirm the recipient’s secure email/FAX address if they ask you to fax — verify personally (call a known number) before sending.

4) Clean up metadata and traces
- After redaction, save as a new file. Remove document properties/metadata (Document > Properties or use a “Sanitize”/“Remove metadata” tool).
- If you printed and marked by hand, scan the printed copy (so original electronic text isn’t embedded) and verify the printed redaction obscured the characters fully.

5) Quick checklist before sending
- Does recipient require full SSN or only last 4? — If only last 4, redact remaining digits.
- Use a proper redaction tool or flatten the image.
- Remove SSN from filename/subject/body.
- Remove metadata.
- Use secure transmission (portal/encrypted file or encrypted email).
- Verify recipient identity/contact method.

