- Ask the recipient whether the last four will suffice before sending a full SSN.

2. Preferred redaction/masking approaches (don’t rely on visual covering)
- Best (digital): Use a proper PDF redaction tool (e.g., Adobe Acrobat’s Redact feature, or a verified redaction feature in your scanner software). True redaction permanently removes the underlying text.
- If working with images: permanently edit the image to remove the digits (erase/pixelate and then save a new file). Don’t just place a black box on top of the text layer without flattening; the original data may still be recoverable.
- Avoid: whiteout, screen overlays, or “covering” text in a PDF without using a redaction tool — these can leave the sensitive data in the file.

3. Masking examples (use these instead of the full number)
- Mask the SSN like: XXX-XX-1234 or ***-**-1234, or display only “last 4: 1234” (replace 1234 with the actual last four).
