Practical guidance

1) Decide what’s required
- Confirm with the requester whether they truly need the full SSN or whether the last four digits will do. Many organizations accept only the last 4.
- If they insist on the full SSN, ask for a secure upload portal or another secure channel (see below) instead of regular email.

2) How to redact correctly (do not just cover with a translucent box)
- Best: use a dedicated PDF redaction feature (e.g., Adobe Acrobat Pro’s Redact tool). Proper redaction removes the text from the file permanently.
- If you don’t have a redaction tool:
  - Print the document, black out the SSN with an opaque permanent marker, then scan the blacked-out paper. (Make sure the ink is truly opaque.)
  - OR open the scan in an image editor, paint solid black over the digits, then save/export as a flattened image or PDF (not a layered file). Confirm the text cannot be selected or copied.
  - OR take a photo of the page after physically redacting it and save the photo as a new file.
- Don’t just place a black rectangle annotation on the PDF without flattening — some annotations/layers can be removed and the underlying text recovered.

3) Verify redaction
- After redaction, try selecting/copying text from the file and searching for the SSN (or any digit sequence) to confirm it’s gone.
- Open the file in another viewer to make sure the digits are not recoverable.
- Check and remove metadata if the file might contain sensitive info in properties.

4) Secure transmission
- Use the requester's secure upload portal when available.
- If you must email, password-protect/encrypt the PDF and send the password by a separate channel (phone call or SMS).
- Use an encrypted file-transfer service or secure email (S/MIME, TLS-encrypted business email, or a secure file share).
- Limit recipients (CC/BCC) and confirm the correct recipient address before sending.

5) Minimize exposure and keep records
- Only send pages that are necessary — remove or redact other personal information (DOB, account numbers, etc.) if not required.
- Keep a record of what you sent and to whom. Delete local copies if not needed.
- If you used an online redaction or conversion service, use a reputable one and delete the upload afterward.

If you tell me how you’re creating the scan (phone photo, scanner) and which tools you have (Adobe Acrobat Pro, Preview on Mac, Windows, etc.), I can give step‑by‑step redaction instructions for that tool or walk you through verifying the redaction. I can also help draft a short message to the requester asking whether the last four digits are sufficient.

